From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: S/PDIF is SPI 23 and 24; SPI 21 has no known owner

The spdif@2036000 node came with 0024 and carries GIC_SPI 21, the same
number 0024 gave cpu-comm@3003000. 0024a moved cpu_comm to 46 and called
21 "the S/PDIF interrupt", on the strength of this node alone; 0024d
repeated that in its comment. It is not: the stock device trees of the
HY310, the HY200 and the HY300 T08 all give the node at 0x02036000
<0 0x17 4>, SPI 23, and none of their nodes owns SPI 21.

What was measured on the HY310 stands (doku/66 section 4): requested as
SPI 21, the line fired 100000 times and the kernel disabled it; on SPI 46
the counter stayed at 0 and there was no storm. So 21 is asserted all the
time on this SoC, by a source nobody has named yet. Only the attribution
to S/PDIF was wrong.

The second node, spdif@2037000, carries SPI 38 from the same origin. The
same three stock trees give 0x02037000 <0 0x18 4>, SPI 24; their SPI 38
belongs to nand0@04011000. This node has a compatible the mainline driver
binds (sun50i-h6-spdif) and is "okay" in the dtsi; the HY310 tree and
every board that includes it switch it off, the HY200 QZ713_V2 tree does
not. No sound card refers to it on any board.

The first number was noticed by cstenger (his review of 14.11.2026, which
checked the stock trees); the second fell out of reading the same nodes.
The comment in cpu-comm@3003000 says what is known. Built with dtc: the
two interrupt properties change in all eight H713 DTBs and nothing else
does. Not booted; neither S/PDIF port has been run under this kernel.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -995,7 +995,7 @@
 		spdif: spdif@2036000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-owa";
 			reg = <0x02036000 0x58>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 21 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 23 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_PLL_AUDIO>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_BUS_OWA0>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_OWA0_TX>,
@@ -1013,7 +1013,7 @@
 		spdif1: spdif@2037000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h6-spdif";
 			reg = <0x02037000 0x58>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 38 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 24 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_OWA1>, <&ccu CLK_OWA1_TX>;
 			clock-names = "apb", "spdif";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_OWA1>;
@@ -2271,8 +2271,10 @@
 			 * device tree lists them: bank 0 @0x03003000 (this
 			 * core's inbox) = 46, bank 1 @0x03003400 (CPUS/ARISC)
 			 * = 109, bank 2 @0x03003800 (display MIPS) = 108.
-			 * 21 is S/PDIF and was the wrong number here until
-			 * 0024a. The driver takes them by index.
+			 * 21 was the wrong number here until 0024a: a line
+			 * that is asserted all the time and that no node of
+			 * the stock device tree owns (S/PDIF is 23 and 24).
+			 * The driver takes them by index.
 			 */
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 46 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				     <GIC_SPI 109 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
